{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=1-\\text{i}\\sqrt{3}$ in exponential form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-\\sqrt{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8079" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0"} {"question" "q-8079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{4\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] ["math" "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=4\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8079" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/83c490278bec718da1338f8926e9d67d2f72909487b9a85bbd386cbf72def2bb.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-4+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{4})| \\\\  & ≈2.897.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\theta =2.897$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.245\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.245\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-8083" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.897\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=-4-3\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{4})| \\\\  & ≈\\pi +0.643\\,50… \\\\  & ≈3.785.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=5$ and $\\theta =3.785$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.434\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.857\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17519" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\text{i}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Write the complex number $z=-2+6\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6817cff3d59030ae52c31cbe6cce1976efecf258b0407977fee39bebe2c5fca0"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}"] ["math" "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-17524" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/state.json" "file_sha256" "4da1e400df857180e9a5a3b5db38886fc4185aa29cc96aab433e99e2697b83be"} {"question" "q-71978" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refe